1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,133
Meet Sunrise Coffee Roasters, a small coffee roaster in Bandung.

2
00:00:04,433 --> 00:00:10,145
About a hundred documents a month: statements, a ledger, invoices and receipts.

3
00:00:10,445 --> 00:00:13,092
But October cost more than it should have.

4
00:00:13,392 --> 00:00:15,947
A missing record? A mistake? Or fraud?

5
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:25,382
Organizations lose about 5% of revenue to fraud each year; for small businesses, the median case costs $141,000.

6
00:00:25,682 --> 00:00:28,004
And checking every page by hand takes days.

7
00:00:28,267 --> 00:00:29,939
That's where Kredibel comes in.

8
00:00:30,239 --> 00:00:35,022
It reads every document, reconciles every month, and shows the evidence behind every number.

9
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,179
Anyone can try the demo account, no Google account needed.

10
00:00:38,479 --> 00:00:41,173
Kredibel first asks what you want.

11
00:00:41,473 --> 00:00:43,748
Our owner wants to check a hunch.

12
00:00:44,048 --> 00:00:51,014
September: 820 million in, 840 million out. October: a billion in, 620 million out.

13
00:00:51,846 --> 00:00:55,422
The dashboard checks the books against those expectations.

14
00:00:55,722 --> 00:01:01,016
September is as expected; October's money out is 86 million over.

15
00:01:01,316 --> 00:01:04,427
And 95 percent of bank lines were matched automatically.

16
00:01:04,695 --> 00:01:08,782
So where did the money go? Here is every October bank line.

17
00:01:09,082 --> 00:01:14,701
Its category, IFRS and US GAAP class, subledger and match.

18
00:01:15,001 --> 00:01:19,041
Even a cash deposit is explained: the ledger books it to sales.

19
00:01:19,328 --> 00:01:22,997
Each month reconciles itself, whatever order the files arrived in.

20
00:01:23,297 --> 00:01:27,244
Every match has its reason; the risk is explained with citations.

21
00:01:27,528 --> 00:01:29,804
The risk page finds what the owner feared.

22
00:01:30,104 --> 00:01:33,958
October is high: a supplier was paid into a new bank account.

23
00:01:34,258 --> 00:01:38,623
August is critical: a statement was edited in a PDF editor.

24
00:01:38,923 --> 00:01:43,149
One amount is in another font; the balance no longer adds up.

25
00:01:43,411 --> 00:01:48,473
Files arrive in any order: a late July invoice, a receipt photo, and a statement copy.

26
00:01:48,773 --> 00:01:52,302
The copy is spotted at once, never counted twice.

27
00:01:52,602 --> 00:01:54,599
Gemini reads each new page.

28
00:01:54,899 --> 00:01:58,475
And code checks each value is on the page before it counts.

29
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:03,414
Anything Kredibel can't decide for certain goes to one review queue.

30
00:02:03,714 --> 00:02:06,918
A held copy, an unpaid invoice, a value to check.

31
00:02:07,187 --> 00:02:11,506
Every AI decision is a label to confirm or correct.

32
00:02:11,806 --> 00:02:16,218
And every run is traced: each Gemini call, its tokens and its cost.

33
00:02:17,487 --> 00:02:19,902
And you can simply ask the books.

34
00:02:20,202 --> 00:02:23,917
The assistant answers from the books' own figures, and cites each one.

35
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:28,891
Ready to try your own books? Sign in with Google.

36
00:02:29,191 --> 00:02:34,160
Set up your business once: its name, industry, currency and time zone.

37
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:37,107
The free trial starts in a workspace of your own.

38
00:02:39,126 --> 00:02:51,525
Kredibel runs on Google Cloud: Firebase Hosting and Authentication, Cloud Run for the app and its ADK workflows, Firestore for the books, and Gemini with Document AI.

39
00:02:51,825 --> 00:02:56,005
Try the demo, or your own books. Kredibel: every number has a source.
